{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VFH6kRcgzm8XFS6tVu8uSq","type":"tool_result","content":"[{\"headword\":\"لَغَوَ \",\"definitions_text\":\"(لَغَوَ) اللَّامُ وَالْغَيْنُ وَالْحَرْفُ الْمُعْتَلُّ أَصْلَانِ صَحِيحَانِ، أَحَدُهُمَا يَدُلُّ عَلَى الشَّيْءِ لَا يُعْتَدُّ بِهِ، وَالْآخَرُ عَلَى اللَّهَجِ بِالشَّيْءِ.\\nفَالْأَوَّلُ اللَّغْوُ: مَا لَا يُعْتَدُّ بِهِ مِنْ أَوْلَادِ الْإِبِلِ فِي الدِّيَةِ. قَالَ الْعَبْدِيُّ:\\nأَوْ مِائَةٍ تُجْعَلُ أَوْلَادُهَا لَغْوًا ... وَعُرْضَ الْمِائَةِ الْجَلْمَدِ\\nيُقَالُ مِنْهُ لَغَا يَلْغُو لَغْوًا. وَذَلِكَ فِي لَغْوِ الْأَيْمَانِ. وَاللَّغَا هُوَ اللَّغْوُ بِعَيْنِهِ. قَالَ اللَّهُ تَعَالَى: {لَا يُؤَاخِذُكُمُ اللَّهُ بِاللَّغْوِ فِي أَيْمَانِكُمْ} [البقرة: 225] ، أَيْ مَا لَمْ تَعْقِدُوهُ بِقُلُوبِكُمْ. وَالْفُقَهَاءُ يَقُولُونَ: هُوَ قَوْلُ الرَّجُلِ لَا وَاللَّهِ، وَبَلَى وَاللَّهِ. وَقَوْمٌ يَقُولُونَ: هُوَ قَوْلُ الرَّجُلِ لِسَوَادٍ مُقْبِلًا: وَاللَّهِ إِنَّ هَذَا فُلَانٌ، يَظُنُّهُ إِيَّاهُ، ثُمَّ لَا يَكُونُ كَمَا ظَنَّ. قَالُوا: فَيَمِينُهُ لَغْوٌ، لِأَنَّهُ لَمْ يَتَعَمَّدِ الْكَذِبَ.\\nوَالثَّانِي قَوْلُهُمْ: لَغِيَ بِالْأَمْرِ، إِذَا لَهِجَ بِهِ. وَيُقَالُ إِنَّ اشْتِقَاقَ اللُّغَةِ مِنْهُ، أَيْ يَلْهَجُ صَاحِبُهَا بِهَا.\"}]","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"43ddaf95-6704-4bc3-bdd3-886d109dc3b2","uuid":"ab94533b-7a44-4914-8ec0-d2746975133d","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"[{\"headword\":\"لَغَوَ \",\"definitions_text\":\"(لَغَوَ) اللَّامُ وَالْغَيْنُ وَالْحَرْفُ الْمُعْتَلُّ أَصْلَانِ صَحِيحَانِ، أَحَدُهُمَا يَدُلُّ عَلَى الشَّيْءِ لَا يُعْتَدُّ بِهِ، وَالْآخَرُ عَلَى اللَّهَجِ بِالشَّيْءِ.\\nفَالْأَوَّلُ اللَّغْوُ: مَا لَا يُعْتَدُّ بِهِ مِنْ أَوْلَادِ الْإِبِلِ فِي الدِّيَةِ. قَالَ الْعَبْدِيُّ:\\nأَوْ مِائَةٍ تُجْعَلُ أَوْلَادُهَا لَغْوًا ... وَعُرْضَ الْمِائَةِ الْجَلْمَدِ\\nيُقَالُ مِنْهُ لَغَا يَلْغُو لَغْوًا. وَذَلِكَ فِي لَغْوِ الْأَيْمَانِ. وَاللَّغَا هُوَ اللَّغْوُ بِعَيْنِهِ. قَالَ اللَّهُ تَعَالَى: {لَا يُؤَاخِذُكُمُ اللَّهُ بِاللَّغْوِ فِي أَيْمَانِكُمْ} [البقرة: 225] ، أَيْ مَا لَمْ تَعْقِدُوهُ بِقُلُوبِكُمْ. وَالْفُقَهَاءُ يَقُولُونَ: هُوَ قَوْلُ الرَّجُلِ لَا وَاللَّهِ، وَبَلَى وَاللَّهِ. وَقَوْمٌ يَقُولُونَ: هُوَ قَوْلُ الرَّجُلِ لِسَوَادٍ مُقْبِلًا: وَاللَّهِ إِنَّ هَذَا فُلَانٌ، يَظُنُّهُ إِيَّاهُ، ثُمَّ لَا يَكُونُ كَمَا ظَنَّ. قَالُوا: فَيَمِينُهُ لَغْوٌ، لِأَنَّهُ لَمْ يَتَعَمَّدِ الْكَذِبَ.\\nوَالثَّانِي قَوْلُهُمْ: لَغِيَ بِالْأَمْرِ، إِذَا لَهِجَ بِهِ. وَيُقَالُ إِنَّ اشْتِقَاقَ اللُّغَةِ مِنْهُ، أَيْ يَلْهَجُ صَاحِبُهَا بِهَا.\"}]","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_01XBDbtTEPSuB1EswZsxSrLC","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have all the evidence I need. Let me compile the full YAML review.\n\n**Key analysis summary:**\n\n**Stage 1 Blind Candidates (before seeing existing lemmas):**\n1. الثَّرْوَةُ اللُّغَوِيَّة (tarkib/wasfi)\n2. مَخْزُونُ الأَلْفَاظ (tarkib/idafi)\n3. المَادَّةُ اللُّغَوِيَّة (majaz/tarkib)\n4. اللَّفِيظَة (ishtiqaq from لفظ)\n\n\n5. ذخيرة لغوية appears in the existing lemmas with a clear linguistic definition from المعجم الكبير describing it as a repertory of phonetic or written symbols within a defined linguistic system.\n\n6. The next thinking shows that while ذخيرة لغوية is indeed used in Arabic linguistics, it typically refers to \"repertoire\" rather than \"lexis\" — the root ذخر fundamentally means storing or preserving something, which aligns with the concept of a speaker's available linguistic resources.\n\n7. The evidence is mixed: the term exists in Arabic linguistic usage but its primary meaning leans toward repertoire rather than the narrower concept of lexicon.\n\n8. Moving to مفردات اللغة, I'm finding consistent confirmation across multiple sources that this term directly corresponds to vocabulary — the entries from agricultural, educational, and modern reference materials all confirm that مفردات means vocabulary, and the root فرد indicates singularity or individual units, which perfectly captures the concept of individual words making up a language's vocabulary stock.\n\nThe remaining candidates (الثروة اللغوية, مخزون الألفاظ, المادة اللغوية, اللفيظة) all show no material found, so I'm moving forward to ذخيرة لغوية. The evidence here is mixed — while ذخيرة in linguistic contexts refers more precisely to a repertoire rather than the totality of words, it's still confirmed as a term used in Arabic linguistics for the aggregate of linguistic units. I need to update the lemma with proper diacritization to ذَخِيرَة لُغَوِيَّة and note that this term emphasizes the curated or available collection aspect.\n\nFor مفردات اللغة, the evidence is straightforward confirmation — this term directly refers to the complete set of lexical and functional units in a language, making it broader and more comprehensive in usage.\n\nNow I'm evaluating several other candidates: ثروة لغوية gets removed because the core concept can be substituted with synonyms like \"غنى\" or \"كنز\" without losing validity; مخزون الألفاظ is descriptive rather than terminological; المادة اللغوية refers specifically to linguistic material in morphology; and لفيظة lacks established usage and material support.\n\nFor the definition itself, I need to move beyond the English translation and develop a proper terminological definition that captures the essence more precisely.\n\nNow I'm refining the core definition to emphasize the totality of linguistic units—both meaningful words and functional grammatical elements—that constitute a language's inventory. The linguistic definition frames this as the accumulated stock of a particular language's lexical and functional resources.\n\nI'm beginning to examine the enrichment stage, starting with ذخيرة لغوية as a potential multiword expression, tracing its etymological roots and semantic foundations. Now I'm examining the etymological roots of individual vocabulary words, breaking down how \"مفردات\" derives from the root فرد, which fundamentally denotes singularity or unity according to classical linguistic analysis.\n\nI'm also distinguishing between two key semantic nuances: the first emphasizes the accumulated linguistic reservoir as a stored and inherited system, while the second focuses on vocabulary as discrete, countable lexical units that can be documented and catalogued.\n\nNow I'm reconsidering the cultural fit classification. While \"مفردات اللغة\" naturally expresses the concept of all words in a language, \"lexis\" as a technical linguistic term lacks a precise single-word Arabic equivalent—the existing multi-word expression is descriptive rather than terminological. I think `phraset` better captures this situation.\n\nActually, wait—I'm second-guessing myself. The synset uses multi-word expressions for both lemmas, so I need to decide which classification fits best. The concept is recognized in Arabic but doesn't have a dedicated term, which points to `lexical_gap`. Let me go with that and move on to writing out the full YAML structure.\n\nFor the definition itself, the current version is clear but a bit wordy—the second part about word forms is somewhat redundant. I'm refining it to be more concise and aligned with the Waseet dictionary style: grouping all the linguistic units in a language, encompassing both those with lexical meaning and those serving grammatical functions. Let me verify this hits the key elements—it has the genus (collection of linguistic units in a language), the differentia (lexical vs. grammatical), and it's not circular.\n\nNow I'm moving to the linguistic definition and then preparing the YAML structure for the updates. Since \"ذخيرة لغوية\" and \"مفردات اللغة\" are existing lemmas that need diacritization, I'll need update actions for both, then update the main definition and set the metadata.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5803,"cache_read_input_tokens":52899,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5803},"output_tokens":10,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"43ddaf95-6704-4bc3-bdd3-886d109dc3b2","uuid":"8ebbe400-9a5c-45e0-b46c-31b1f6fe5b6f"}
